## Hardware Pinout Configuration (SPI Bus)

The micro SD card slot on this DIYmalls 3.5" ESP32-S3 (JC3248W535C) development board communicates using the standard **SPI (Serial Peripheral Interface)** bus. The data lines are shared across the hardware platform, using standard 4-wire synchronization rules:

| Signal Name | ESP32-S3 GPIO | Description |
|:---|:---:|:---|
| **SD_CS** | **10** | Chip Select (Active Low listener trigger) |
| **SD_MOSI** | **11** | Master Out Slave In (Data line from ESP32 to SD Card) |
| **SD_MISO** | **13** | Master In Slave Out (Data line from SD Card to ESP32) |
| **SD_SCK** | **12** | Serial Clock (Synchronizing system hardware beat) |

